1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:04,040
As usual, Dear Uncle believed the English had a hand in it,

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:08,980
but Aziz-Saltaneh suspected her own husband, Dustali Khan,

3
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,675
and fired a loaded gun at him.

4
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:15,900
Terrified of his wife, Dustali Khan hid in Dear Uncle's house

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:19,940
and pretended he had no hope of surviving.

6
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:23,835
Fearing a scandal, Aziz-Saltaneh

7
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:38,960
had apparently believed the fiendish Allahverdi, the Indian Sardar's ex-servant,

8
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:43,160
so the family's centuries-old honor would stay intact.

9
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,540
Why should I lie, Sir? The grave is this close!

10
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:57,080
True, our fellow townsman really has his eye on Lady Qamar,

11
00:02:57,120 --> 00:03:01,380
but when it comes to honor, put all of Iran on one side,

12
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:04,725
and Ghias Abad on the other!

13
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:06,680
We had a fellow townsman...

14
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:09,480
Stop yapping, damn you and your townsman!

15
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:11,380
You had a fellow townsman again?!

16
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,160
Oh, let him have his say!

17
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:16,650
Don't you want to get out of this mess you've made?

18
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:17,580
Go on, Mash Ghasem.

19
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:20,120
Yes, Sir.

20
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:24,540
Yes, Sir, we had a townsman who'd married off two sons.

21
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:29,020
Then one day he heard that before their wedding, at the shrine,

22
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:32,820
his wife's chador had slipped off her head. He divorced her!

23
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:37,440
Even so, all the Ghias Abadis taunted him for not cutting her head off!

24
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:41,420
From that day on, he was known as dishonorable.

25
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:45,025
Three days later he died of shame.

26
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:51,740
I'm telling you so you don't think you can saddle our townsman with Lady Qamar!

27
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:55,480
Now, no need to tell him about Qamar's pregnancy.

28
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:57,520
Why would we?

29
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:59,760
You think Ghias Abadis are such donkeys?

30
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,920
Moment, Mash Ghasem!

31
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:06,680
If nobody says anything, how will your townsman find out?

32
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:10,400
But, Sir, why should I lie? The grave is this close!

33
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,980
No offense, we don't know about Tehran folk,

34
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:17,780
but in Ghias Abad, women and girls are a bit different.

35
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:21,530
Merci, Mash Ghasem. Thanks for the information.

36
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:26,040
If I'm not mistaken, you mean Ghias Abad's women have been to San Francisco,

37
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,900
but their daughters haven't.

38
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:30,540
Bravo! That's just what we meant.

39
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:33,240
Mr. Aspiran might not realize at first,

40
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:36,460
but being a Ghias Abadi, he'll realize on the wedding night.

41
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:37,180
Moment!

42
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:41,060
But given how protective of honor Ghias Abadis are,

43
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:45,120
I don't think Mr. Aspiran will go up on the roof and shout it.

44
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:50,020
I think even if he finds out, at most he'll divorce her.

45
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:52,240
Isn't that exactly what you want?

46
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:54,320
Someone marries Qamar,

47
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:56,140
and days later quietly divorces her.

48
00:04:56,180 --> 00:05:01,220
That's base, unconscionable! He must be told about the baby up front!

49
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:06,460
You have to pick one.

50
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,160
Son-in-law or conscience!

51
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,750
Let's take a vote.

52
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,340
I vote for the son-in-law.

53
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,240
And you, Mr. Dustali,

54
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:15,800
Lord of Conscience,

55
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,520
vote for conscience.

56
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,800
In defense of my position, I say

57
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,940
that nothing unconscionable

58
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:23,460
is being done.

59
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:24,920
The Ghias Abadi Aspiran

60
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,280
eats and sleeps free for a few days,

61
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:29,620
becomes Aziz-Saltaneh's son-in-law,

62
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:31,990
doesn't spend a penny,

63
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:35,220
and gets a free trip to San Francisco!

64
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:37,280
I'd move to Ghias Abad for that!

65
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:41,320
God willing, may God grant you and me such luck!

66
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,300
You were conceived in liquor and wine!

67
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:46,720
Moment!

68
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:50,160
And you, conceived in holy water and rosewater,

69
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:52,380
would you hate them paying your way,

70
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:54,300
begging you to accept,

71
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:57,220
feeding you free lunch and dinner,

72
00:05:57,260 --> 00:06:00,260
and with a plump young companion

73
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,880
sending you to San Francisco for a few days, huh?

74
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:05,260
If it stings, say ouch!

75
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,700
What drivel is this?

76
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:08,280
To hell with your ugly faces!

77
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:11,720
Has my daughter sunk so low you must beg that Ghias Abadi?

78
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:14,746
Was my daughter born in a ditch?

79
00:06:14,796 --> 00:06:16,440
Don't get angry, Madam.

80
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:19,560
Granted, Lady Qamar wasn't born in a ditch,

81
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,420
maybe the Aspiran won't want a wife.

82
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:22,780
And even if he does,

83
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,860
maybe Qamar herself won't want him.

84
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:25,940
Qamar wouldn't dare!

85
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:28,560
Then, Lady Aziz, let's go talk to Qamar,

86
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:30,260
and if she agrees, I'll send Mash Ghasem

87
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:33,200
to the Aspiran before it's too late.

88
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:34,280
But...

89
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:38,210
But this poor girl of mine doesn't understand a thing.

90
00:06:39,436 --> 00:06:40,900
Whenever I ask her something,

91
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:42,480
she just talks nonsense. Gibberish.

92
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,480
Will you let me go and talk to her?

93
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:46,180
You won't get anything out of her.

94
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:47,700
God strike me dead!

95
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:51,140
Since this disaster struck her, she's completely lost her mind.

96
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:53,445
I'll go talk her into it.

97
00:07:08,016 --> 00:07:10,411
Well, well! Two pretty ladies!

98
00:07:13,976 --> 00:07:16,186
What are you knitting, Qamar dear?

99
00:07:16,236 --> 00:07:19,126
Qamar's knitting a sweater for her baby.

100
00:07:19,176 --> 00:07:21,420
Moment! How's that?

101
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:22,700
I didn't catch that.

102
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:24,520
For her baby?

103
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:27,020
Qamar dreamt of her baby last night.

104
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:29,380
She says it wore a red sweater, right, Qamar?

105
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:32,460
Yes, it was wearing a red sweater.

106
00:07:41,396 --> 00:07:44,780
Well, since you love babies,

107
00:07:46,396 --> 00:07:48,020
you have to get married.

108
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:51,440
A baby can't go without a father, you know.

109
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,220
No.

110
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,360
I don't want to. I love babies.

111
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:55,620
I don't want a husband.

112
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:58,080
She says her baby likes this color.

113
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,660
Yes, it does.

114
00:08:01,776 --> 00:08:06,336
Listen, Qamar dear, as it happens, we've found you a nice husband.

115
00:08:06,696 --> 00:08:09,936
The baby wants her to knit it a red sweater.

116
00:08:10,776 --> 00:08:14,595
Well, sweetheart, knit a pretty sweater for your husband too.

117
00:08:14,635 --> 00:08:16,686
A baby needs a daddy.

118
00:08:16,736 --> 00:08:20,356
If you have no husband, the baby will be sad.

119
00:08:20,536 --> 00:08:23,346
All children love having a daddy.

120
00:08:23,396 --> 00:08:24,486
All right.

121
00:08:24,536 --> 00:08:27,906
Then you buy me yarn, and I'll knit its daddy a sweater too.

122
00:08:27,956 --> 00:08:29,346
Of course I will.

123
00:08:29,396 --> 00:08:30,346
What color?

124
00:08:30,396 --> 00:08:32,356
Red too.

125
00:08:32,736 --> 00:08:35,666
Then we must get the wedding going, Leili dear!

126
00:08:35,716 --> 00:08:38,876
What do you think Qamar's wedding dress

127
00:08:39,016 --> 00:08:40,806
should look like? What color?

128
00:08:40,856 --> 00:08:43,610
A long white dress with a pretty veil.

129
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:45,660
With orange blossoms.

130
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:47,620
Bravo!

131
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:50,660
Right, a row of orange blossoms here.

132
00:08:50,856 --> 00:08:51,686
Lovely!

133
00:08:51,736 --> 00:08:52,726
Yes, that'll look nice.

134
00:08:52,776 --> 00:08:53,526
Uncle Asdollah?

135
00:08:53,576 --> 00:08:54,366
Yes, dear?

136
00:08:54,416 --> 00:08:55,766
So where is he?

137
00:08:55,816 --> 00:08:56,706
Who, dear?

138
00:08:56,756 --> 00:08:57,806
My husband.

139
00:08:57,856 --> 00:09:00,646
I want him to have thick black hair,

140
00:09:00,696 --> 00:09:04,660
so my baby's hair will be black and long and pretty like his.

141
00:09:08,576 --> 00:09:09,931
Well, honestly...

142
00:09:10,516 --> 00:09:12,620
Well, Leili, you help

143
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:14,620
Qamar finish her sweater,

144
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:16,620
while I go set up the wedding.

145
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:18,620
Here comes the bride!

146
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:20,925
All dressed in white!

147
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:30,620
Poor thing.

148
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:32,620
What a sweet girl.

149
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:34,620
It won't work.

150
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,620
Seems this business just won't work out.

151
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:38,620
Why's that?

152
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:40,620
Because we heard with our own ears

153
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:42,620
Lady Qamar saying

154
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:45,876
she wants her man to have thick hair.

155
00:09:46,496 --> 00:09:47,186
She didn't tell you?

156
00:09:47,236 --> 00:09:48,166
She told me too.

157
00:09:48,216 --> 00:09:50,741
Why, what color is the Aspiran's hair?

158
00:09:51,156 --> 00:09:54,876
Why should I lie, Sir? The grave is this close!

159
00:09:55,316 --> 00:10:00,156
The day we saw this townsman of ours, he had his hat pulled down to here.

160
00:10:00,536 --> 00:10:05,026
But once, when he took his hat off, we caught sight of his head.

161
00:10:05,076 --> 00:10:06,796
Good grief!

162
00:10:06,836 --> 00:10:09,686
Now tell me, was his hair black or not?

163
00:10:10,616 --> 00:10:12,610
Why should I lie, Sir? Seems like

164
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:15,466
it was every color.

165
00:10:15,516 --> 00:10:19,211
A few strands were white, a few were henna red,

166
00:10:19,636 --> 00:10:21,666
and the rest were black.

167
00:10:21,716 --> 00:10:28,660
When he took his hat off, his scalp was bald from north to south, east to west!

168
00:10:29,736 --> 00:10:34,426
God strike me dead! My child will die seeing a head like that in her arms!

169
00:10:34,476 --> 00:10:36,416
She'll faint from fright.

170
00:10:36,936 --> 00:10:39,620
Madam, the Aspiran isn't Rudolph Valentino.

171
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:43,160
We'll buy him a wig so his head won't show.

172
00:10:43,376 --> 00:10:45,180
Now that, seems like, he won't accept.

173
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:47,800
Ghias Abadis are very protective of their honor.

174
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,060
What are you saying?

175
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:52,140
Moment... Do Ghias Abadis keep their honor on their scalps?

176
00:10:52,180 --> 00:10:54,250
Why should I lie, Sir?

177
00:10:56,016 --> 00:10:58,506
Moment, moment... -The grave is this close!

178
00:10:58,556 --> 00:10:59,700
Leave his hair to me.

179
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:02,440
When can you find your townsman and talk to him?

180
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,160
Huh? Tell me, when?

181
00:11:04,916 --> 00:11:06,480
Whenever you say, Sir.

182
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,220
I'm afraid this Mash Ghasem will scare the fellow off.

183
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:11,360
We must find a way.

184
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:14,000
How about we call the chief of police

185
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:17,400
and have him make up an excuse to send the Aspiran here on duty?

186
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,280
How about it?

187
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,000
Good idea.

188
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:21,160
Have you lot gone mad?

189
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,870
Do you realize what you're doing?

190
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:27,160
Calling the chief of police

191
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:29,880
to find Mr. Ghias Abadi

192
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:33,880
and send him here to marry Sir's uncle's granddaughter?

193
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,560
What brilliant minds you both have!

194
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:39,960
Asdollah, how many bottles of arak have you had since morning?

195
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,020
Me, Sir? I'm not drunk.

196
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:44,220
The Aspiran has to come here eventually.

197
00:11:44,260 --> 00:11:46,480
You can't propose to him over the phone!

198
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:47,940
Lady Aziz, it's a good idea.

199
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:49,700
Call and get him to come here.

200
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:51,620
Say, for instance, a watch is missing.

201
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:53,680
You don't want an official complaint,

202
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:55,460
you just want an officer to come

203
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,260
and quietly question your maids and servants.

204
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:00,380
Then ask for the Aspiran if possible.

205
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,700
These things go faster as a friendly favor.

206
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:05,220
When the Aspiran gets here, say the watch turned up.

207
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:07,140
Then grab him and marry her off to him.

208
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,260
Hurry, Lady Aziz, run and call!

209
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:11,560
Good idea. Let's hope the chief is in.

210
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:12,695
Yes.

211
00:12:16,226 --> 00:12:18,600
Suppose the chief agrees,

212
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:20,600
what if he sends someone else?

213
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:24,640
Even better! I doubt the police has a single officer uglier than the Aspiran.

214
00:12:25,266 --> 00:12:27,600
Now where are you off to, Asdollah?

215
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:31,640
I'll be right back, Sir. I've other business besides marrying off women.

216
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:39,416
Whoever they send, keep him here till I'm back to hitch Qamar to him.

217
00:12:39,466 --> 00:12:41,211
Don't let him leave, mind!

218
00:12:46,576 --> 00:12:47,766
Hi, Uncle Asdollah.

219
00:12:47,806 --> 00:12:48,776
You're still here?

220
00:12:48,826 --> 00:12:50,256
So, what's new?

221
00:12:50,306 --> 00:12:53,216
The relatives are meeting tonight to go to the station.

222
00:12:53,266 --> 00:12:55,656
Pouri's coming back from Ahvaz tonight.

223
00:12:55,706 --> 00:12:58,736
And you just sit on your hands and watch.

224
00:12:58,786 --> 00:13:02,926
Boy, there's no problem in the world a trip to San Francisco can't fix.

225
00:13:02,966 --> 00:13:05,290
See how they want to saddle the Aspiran with Qamar.

226
00:13:05,330 --> 00:13:06,130
But I-

227
00:13:06,170 --> 00:13:09,085
Get lost, you useless wimp, you make me sick.

228
00:13:15,466 --> 00:13:16,396
It's done.

229
00:13:16,446 --> 00:13:18,486
What a gem of a man the police chief is.

230
00:13:18,526 --> 00:13:19,326
He agreed.

231
00:13:19,366 --> 00:13:22,916
He said he'd send the Aspiran himself right away to investigate.

232
00:13:22,966 --> 00:13:24,416
Warn Qamar.

233
00:13:24,466 --> 00:13:27,236
Make sure nothing slips out of her mouth.

234
00:13:27,286 --> 00:13:28,416
No, Sir.

235
00:13:28,466 --> 00:13:33,156
Lady Aziz, we wanted to say, when our townsman comes, leave him be.

236
00:13:33,206 --> 00:13:34,796
We'll win him over ourselves.

237
00:13:34,846 --> 00:13:38,036
We'll get the hair business across to him somehow.

238
00:13:38,086 --> 00:13:41,316
A Ghias Abadi speaks Ghias Abadi.

239
00:13:41,366 --> 00:13:43,616
Don't you bring up his hair.

240
00:13:43,666 --> 00:13:44,856
Leave that to me.

241
00:13:44,906 --> 00:13:48,276
If he hears the word "wig," he'll never go along, mind.

242
00:13:48,326 --> 00:13:49,076
You've been warned.

243
00:13:49,126 --> 00:13:50,296
Oh, oh, to hell with it!

244
00:13:50,346 --> 00:13:52,906
Now I have to pander to this stinking baldy too!

245
00:13:52,946 --> 00:13:56,946
Damn you, Dustali, for bringing this black day on me!

246
00:13:58,366 --> 00:14:00,706
Oh, what a pretty nightingale!

247
00:14:01,726 --> 00:14:04,316
Slow down, it'll snap!

248
00:14:07,446 --> 00:14:09,446
You've got so much string!

249
00:14:20,486 --> 00:14:24,640
Mash Ghasem, so why won't the Aspiran agree to wear a wig?

250
00:14:25,886 --> 00:14:27,891
He's right, my boy.

251
00:14:28,166 --> 00:14:30,740
Ghias Abadis are second to none in honor.

252
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:34,080
Even these Tehran folk with all their airs and frills,

253
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:38,580
not one in a hundred thousand would wear a wig like a woman.

254
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:42,240
Mash Ghasem, just between us, what's a wig got to do with honor?

255
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:46,040
Bless you, you go to school! What kind of talk is that, my boy?

256
00:14:46,666 --> 00:14:50,666
What could be more shameless than a man wearing a wig like a woman?

257
00:14:51,566 --> 00:14:55,940
What we're telling you, we once saw with our own eyes.

258
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:59,935
One year a troupe came to Ghias Abad to stage a passion play.

259
00:15:00,466 --> 00:15:02,796
One of the women of the Imam's household,

260
00:15:03,026 --> 00:15:04,706
bless them,

261
00:15:05,166 --> 00:15:08,620
was supposed to throw off her chador and tear out her hair.

262
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:12,660
Everyone said we must find a man to wear a wig.

263
00:15:13,266 --> 00:15:15,020
Twenty whole days and nights,

264
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:18,340
a hundred people searched all of Ghias Abad.

265
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:20,460
Not one would stoop to such shamelessness.

266
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,660
Ghasem!

267
00:15:21,906 --> 00:15:25,620
Ghasem, fill that ewer and put it by the privy.

268
00:15:26,246 --> 00:15:27,341
Yes, Sir.

269
00:15:46,926 --> 00:15:48,606
Here you are, Sir.

270
00:15:52,526 --> 00:15:54,940
So do you think the Aspiran will agree?

271
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:58,180
Why should I lie, my boy? The grave is this close!

272
00:15:58,220 --> 00:16:02,680
This Ghias Abadi has lived in Tehran for years now.

273
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,900
Maybe his nature's changed by now,

274
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:08,310
and he does shameless things like that, for all we know.

275
00:16:13,746 --> 00:16:14,506
Silence!

276
00:16:14,546 --> 00:16:15,026
Hello, Mr.-

277
00:16:15,066 --> 00:16:15,796
Your name?

278
00:16:15,836 --> 00:16:16,386
What?

279
00:16:16,426 --> 00:16:17,550
Wh-wh-why lie, Sir...

280
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,040
Lie? Why lie?

281
00:16:19,086 --> 00:16:19,696
Answer!

282
00:16:19,746 --> 00:16:20,896
Quick, fast, swift!

283
00:16:20,946 --> 00:16:22,196
We... we lie...

284
00:16:22,246 --> 00:16:23,556
Why lie? The grave is this-

285
00:16:23,606 --> 00:16:24,586
Silence!

286
00:16:24,626 --> 00:16:25,576
Sir.

287
00:16:25,626 --> 00:16:27,761
His name is Mash Ghasem.

288
00:16:29,706 --> 00:16:31,590
Suspect number two

289
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:35,180
in the previous crime. Mash Ghasem!

290
00:16:36,146 --> 00:16:39,061
Halt! Stay where you are! Halt! Halt! Halt!

291
00:16:39,566 --> 00:16:42,320
Go, go! If the inspector sees you, there'll be trouble.

292
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:45,560
Quiet! Who asked you? Let him speak for himself!

293
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:48,320
Don't be scared, my boy, the Nayeb's just like that.

294
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,200
Quiet! Halt!

295
00:16:52,506 --> 00:16:54,860
Mr. Nayeb Teymoor-Khan, you?

296
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,940
Yes, me in person!

297
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:59,180
I didn't think they'd trouble you.

298
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:02,420
Your Excellency, so tell me, what happened? What's missing?

299
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:12,180
Th-th-the... the late master's watch, watch, watch has g-g-gone missing.

300
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:15,900
Quiet! Time is money. What did you say was missing?

301
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:24,320
The watch... the w-watch, the late master's watch, Aziz-Saltaneh's father's.

302
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:25,420
Gold?

303
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:27,075
Yes, yes, gold.

304
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:31,095
Have you had lunch?

305
00:17:31,246 --> 00:17:32,760
Yes, lunch was four hours ago.

306
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:36,116
Four hours? How do you know it's been four hours since lunch?

307
00:17:36,166 --> 00:17:37,120
Looked at a watch?

308
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:39,000
The late master's watch? Answer!

309
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:39,860
Quick, fast, swift!

310
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:41,880
Seems like you want...

311
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:42,900
you want...

312
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:46,375
God forgive you! Mr. Nayeb, why the accusations?

313
00:17:47,406 --> 00:17:49,200
These servants and staff

314
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:51,040
have each been in our house

315
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:52,600
for twenty, thirty years.

316
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:55,040
Who sent you here anyway?

317
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:57,720
Aspiran Ghias Abadi was supposed to come.

318
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:59,720
Why did you come?

319
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,720
What? I didn't catch that.

320
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:02,736
Go on, mister, beat it.

321
00:18:02,786 --> 00:18:05,720
Insulting a government officer in the line of duty?

322
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:07,760
Come on, move!

323
00:18:10,986 --> 00:18:12,211
Out!

324
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,720
Don't be upset, Mr. Nayeb.

325
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,720
I didn't mean to insult you.

326
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,720
Aziz-Saltaneh has lost

327
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,720
her father's watch.

328
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:23,720
She's upset.

329
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,720
A man's watch isn't something that'd be

330
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,720
in Aziz-Saltaneh's purse to get lost.

331
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,720
The watch was stolen!

332
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:30,720
Theft!

333
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,720
Robbery!

334
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,720
Crime!

335
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:34,720
How can you be so sure?

336
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,720
Who told you?

337
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:38,720
My nose!

338
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:41,720
The nose of Nayeb Teymoor-Khan,

339
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:44,720
inventor of the international surprise system!

340
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:47,612
Hey, hey, don't come, don't come!

341
00:18:47,662 --> 00:18:48,720
Don't! The inspector's here.

342
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,720
Don't come in, the inspector's here!

343
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:52,720
So what? Why should he go?

344
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:53,720
Come in.

345
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:55,050
Yes, sir.

346
00:19:07,422 --> 00:19:09,622
Get out of here. It's unseemly.

347
00:19:22,642 --> 00:19:23,720
And who's this?

348
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:25,895
Brother's servant, the Col-...

349
00:19:26,362 --> 00:19:28,862
Silence!

350
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:36,050
You tell me.

351
00:19:37,562 --> 00:19:39,152
He's Sir's brother's servant.

352
00:19:39,202 --> 00:19:40,362
Yes, sir.

353
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:45,710
Sir, I came to tell you the Colonel said

354
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:50,662
if you're coming to the station to welcome Master Pouri,

355
00:19:50,782 --> 00:19:51,732
the carriage is ready at dusk.

356
00:19:51,772 --> 00:19:52,220
Silence!

357
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:53,060
Yes!

358
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:54,895
Aspiran Ghias Abadi?

359
00:19:55,462 --> 00:19:56,140
Yes, Sir!

360
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:56,880
Confess!

361
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:57,320
Confess!

362
00:19:57,360 --> 00:19:57,900
Confess!

363
00:19:57,940 --> 00:19:58,460
Confess!

364
00:19:58,500 --> 00:19:58,740
Quick!

365
00:19:58,740 --> 00:19:59,120
Fast!

366
00:19:59,160 --> 00:19:59,600
Now!

367
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:00,020
Swift!

368
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:00,820
Answer!

369
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:02,860
If you confess, your sentence will be reduced.

370
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:05,320
If you don't, I'll put the noose round your neck myself!

371
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:06,160
Confess!

372
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:07,300
Where's the watch?

373
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:08,180
By Imam Ali,

374
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:08,760
I...

375
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:09,600
I...

376
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,780
I didn't steal it.

377
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:12,360
I found it.

378
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:13,960
I'm telling the truth.

379
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,160
By God, I didn't steal it.

380
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,800
I found it.

381
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:21,260
Nayeb Teymoor-Khan's international surprise system

382
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:23,860
has no equal in the world!

383
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:25,740
Aspiran Ghias Abadi?

384
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:26,380
Yes, Sir!

385
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:28,035
Monument to stupidity!

386
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:29,600
Handcuffs!

387
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:32,260
For God's sake, don't lock me up!

388
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:34,480
By Imam Ali, we didn't steal it!

389
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:36,320
I swear we found it!

390
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,740
Where did you find it? Quick!

391
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:39,680
Fast, swift!

392
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:42,100
It was lying in the alley, and I found it.

393
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:42,940
Where?

394
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,420
In the alley, I swear to God!

395
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:46,420
Oh, good Lord!

396
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:48,400
What? What did you say?

397
00:20:48,980 --> 00:20:50,300
Oh, good Lord!

398
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:55,400
It's the Indian Sardar's watch! Must've fallen out of his pocket in the alley!

399
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:57,770
He'd accused the shoeshine man!

400
00:20:58,502 --> 00:21:01,640
It fell out when he grappled with the shoeshine man.

401
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:04,040
What? A fight? Indian? Shoeshine man? What's this?

402
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:07,080
Bless you, you won't let us get a word in!

403
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:08,240
Talk! Quick, fast, swift!

404
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:09,940
Seems like we forgot.

405
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,640
What did you ask?

406
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:14,300
You said Indian, fight, shoeshine man, what's this?

407
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:15,732
Indian, fight, shoeshine...

408
00:21:15,782 --> 00:21:17,202
Oh, good Lord!

409
00:21:17,862 --> 00:21:18,620
We're muddled.

410
00:21:18,660 --> 00:21:19,440
We forgot.

411
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:20,965
Don't be afraid, Ghasem.

412
00:21:21,442 --> 00:21:23,920
Actually, Mr. Nayeb, this Ghasem...

413
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:26,460
Silence!

414
00:21:33,062 --> 00:21:33,820
Now speak.

415
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:36,220
This neighbor of ours,

416
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:38,920
the Indian Sardar Maharat-Khan,

417
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:42,540
got into a fight yesterday with the local shoeshine man.

418
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:45,860
He went to the police station and complained

419
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:48,700
that the shoeshine man had picked his pocket.

420
00:21:48,740 --> 00:21:52,580
Turns out the watch fell out of his pocket in the fight,

421
00:21:53,882 --> 00:21:56,680
and my brother's servant here found it.

422
00:21:56,720 --> 00:22:00,780
Ghasem, take this watch to the station chief,

423
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:03,560
so they'll free this poor wretch sooner.

424
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:06,460
So this wretched watch is to be taken to the station

425
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:08,840
and the stolen goods set free!

426
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:11,782
Who gave this order? You?

427
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:13,675
Or you?

428
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:15,000
You?

429
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,880
Moment... Moment, Mr. Inspector.

430
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:24,140
Tell me, aren't you the killer of Aziz-Saltaneh's murdered husband?

431
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:25,340
Yes!

432
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:30,880
I'm the very killer of Aziz-Saltaneh's murdered husband!

433
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:36,060
Today I'll take revenge on the officer who uncovered my crime!

434
00:22:38,522 --> 00:22:43,060
"Inspector murdered by fiendish killer!" Extra, extra!

435
00:22:46,282 --> 00:22:47,460
Aspiran Ghias Abadi?

436
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:48,760
Yes, Sir? -Handcuffs!

437
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:51,065
Will you let us send him on his way?

438
00:22:52,122 --> 00:22:53,740
Asdollah, no jokes now.

439
00:22:53,780 --> 00:22:55,780
Let this gentleman do his job,

440
00:22:55,820 --> 00:22:57,560
so he'll be out of our hair.

441
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:59,740
What? Me, leave?

442
00:22:59,780 --> 00:23:01,360
Just like that?

443
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:04,580
Then what about Aziz-Saltaneh's stolen watch?

444
00:23:04,620 --> 00:23:06,920
I don't want you finding the watch at all!

445
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:08,880
I don't want... Give it here.

446
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:10,600
Give it here, let me see.

447
00:23:11,442 --> 00:23:12,780
Brother, please... Shamsali!

448
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:14,960
Brother, please, hurry, take this watch to

449
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:15,960
the station chief,

450
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,680
so they'll free that poor wretch sooner.

451
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:20,480
Halt, damn it!

452
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:23,920
Wait till I settle things with you!

453
00:23:26,462 --> 00:23:27,817
What's that?

454
00:23:28,102 --> 00:23:29,340
Well, isn't this lovely!

455
00:23:29,380 --> 00:23:31,280
Insulting a government officer

456
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,180
in the line of duty,

457
00:23:33,220 --> 00:23:35,180
and now intent to commit assault!

458
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:37,940
Telephone... Where's the telephone?

459
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:40,180
I want a word with your chief.

460
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:42,180
I didn't say anything to you.

461
00:23:42,220 --> 00:23:44,912
If you really have no complaint,

462
00:23:44,962 --> 00:23:46,812
well, we'll take our leave.

463
00:23:46,862 --> 00:23:48,180
It's nothing.

464
00:23:48,220 --> 00:23:49,180
Aspiran Ghias Abadi?

465
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:50,180
Yes, Sir!

466
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:51,180
Monument to stupidity!

467
00:23:51,220 --> 00:23:52,380
Move!

468
00:23:53,942 --> 00:23:56,170
Move what? Wait, sir.

469
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:58,792
The watch business has to be cleared up.

470
00:23:58,842 --> 00:24:01,820
Someone has to investigate this, my dear man.

471
00:24:01,860 --> 00:24:05,560
I'd love to put the noose round your neck myself!

472
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:08,460
Mr. Nayeb Teymoor-Khan, please,

473
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:11,160
the chief wants to speak with you on the phone.

474
00:24:11,202 --> 00:24:12,817
Now you're in for it.

475
00:24:20,430 --> 00:24:22,000
How are you, townsman?

476
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:23,240
Keeping well, God willing?

477
00:24:23,280 --> 00:24:24,620
You haven't come to see us.

478
00:24:24,660 --> 00:24:28,260
How many Ghias Abadis are there in all of Tehran, anyway?

479
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:29,220
True enough.

480
00:24:29,260 --> 00:24:30,590
Aspiran Ghias Abadi?

481
00:24:30,630 --> 00:24:31,430
Yes, Sir!

482
00:24:31,470 --> 00:24:35,100
You stay right here and carry on the search for the lady's watch.

483
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:36,625
Yes, Sir!

484
00:24:39,190 --> 00:24:41,200
For now, the chief has summoned me.

485
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:42,940
The suspect is free.

486
00:24:42,980 --> 00:24:44,400
No kidding?

487
00:24:46,870 --> 00:24:48,140
Why are you so quiet?

488
00:24:48,180 --> 00:24:50,340
What a ridiculous man this Nayeb is!

489
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:51,540
Silence!

490
00:24:51,890 --> 00:24:53,800
We'll begin the investigation.

491
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:56,860
Moment, Mr. Aspiran, no need to rush.

492
00:24:56,900 --> 00:25:00,380
First have some tea, then we'll search at leisure and find it.

493
00:25:00,420 --> 00:25:02,840
I'm sure the lady put the watch somewhere and forgot.

494
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:03,860
Yes, she's right.

495
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:06,940
If someone did steal it, with your brilliant mind

496
00:25:06,980 --> 00:25:08,460
it'll turn up at once.

497
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:11,780
Why, the gentleman's very face shows what a talented man he is.

498
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:13,955
You're too kind, townsman.

499
00:25:14,310 --> 00:25:16,580
I bet in every criminal case,

500
00:25:16,620 --> 00:25:19,240
it's the Aspiran's brains that uncover the truth.

501
00:25:19,280 --> 00:25:21,820
But the credit always goes to that

502
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:23,280
oaf, Nayeb Teymoor-Khan.

503
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:24,780
In brains and understanding,

504
00:25:24,820 --> 00:25:26,600
you're head and shoulders above the Nayeb.

505
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:28,320
I mean it, really.

506
00:25:28,530 --> 00:25:31,280
Of course, it's different for a man with connections

507
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:33,650
than for a man without.

508
00:25:34,380 --> 00:25:35,840
If you really want, mind you,

509
00:25:35,880 --> 00:25:38,280
we've a hundred friends who are ministers and MPs.

510
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:39,640
Bless your kindness.

511
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:43,300
With your brains and talent, it's a shame you don't get ahead.

512
00:25:43,340 --> 00:25:45,750
I thought you'd have become a department head by now.

513
00:25:45,790 --> 00:25:46,590
No, sir.

514
00:25:46,630 --> 00:25:47,250
You haven't?

515
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:50,880
Well, your wife and kids shouldn't suffer for your modesty.

516
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,925
Right, Mr. Aspiran?

517
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:56,640
I'm not married. I mean, I was.

518
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,640
We separated a while ago.

519
00:25:58,680 --> 00:26:02,140
I have a son, who lives with his mother, of course,

520
00:26:02,180 --> 00:26:04,100
but I pay for his upkeep.

521
00:26:04,150 --> 00:26:05,940
He pays for his upkeep?

522
00:26:05,990 --> 00:26:09,990
Mash Ghasem, weren't you supposed to look after Mr. Aspiran?

523
00:26:11,590 --> 00:26:13,640
Come, townsman, down to the cellar, it's cool there.

524
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:16,400
Then what about the lady's watch?

525
00:26:16,850 --> 00:26:19,600
There's time. Come down to the cellar for tea.

526
00:26:19,650 --> 00:26:23,650
Wet your whistle. Come, don't stand on ceremony, come on now.

527
00:26:23,850 --> 00:26:24,640
Please, please.

528
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:25,640
Hello, dear.

529
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:27,680
Come along, come along, townsman.

530
00:26:27,730 --> 00:26:32,030
Don't stand on ceremony, I beg you.

531
00:26:37,130 --> 00:26:38,960
Seems it's getting somewhere.

532
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:42,080
Yes, it's getting me to my wits' end!

533
00:26:46,570 --> 00:26:49,540
Go tell Brother I'm not feeling well,

534
00:26:49,580 --> 00:26:52,365
I can't come to the railway station.

535
00:27:16,930 --> 00:27:20,000
Since the 13th of Mordad, when I fell in love with Leili,

536
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:22,380
Dear Uncle had grown frailer by the day.

537
00:27:22,420 --> 00:27:28,380
At home and outside, he took Agha Jan's relentless, invisible blows.

538
00:27:29,090 --> 00:27:35,540
Heedless of his state, the family sought a husband for Qamar for a few days,

539
00:27:35,580 --> 00:27:39,400
to cover up Dustali Khan's misdeed.

540
00:27:40,730 --> 00:27:47,660
The troubles never ended. Each day a new obstacle rose between Leili and me.

541
00:27:49,790 --> 00:27:52,140
Well, well, look who's back!

542
00:27:52,180 --> 00:27:56,080
Houshang Khan, if you knew how upset we were...

543
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:59,480
Thank God the misunderstanding's cleared up.

544
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,320
God bless you, sir.

545
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:03,020
We came here to earn a living.

546
00:28:03,060 --> 00:28:06,495
That bastard Indian accused us of theft.

547
00:28:06,930 --> 00:28:08,860
The godless wretch got us a night in jail.

548
00:28:08,900 --> 00:28:10,220
Don't be upset.

549
00:28:10,260 --> 00:28:14,020
God himself gives such people what they deserve.

550
00:28:14,060 --> 00:28:15,900
I'll settle his account myself, sir.

551
00:28:15,940 --> 00:28:19,320
When the time comes, I know what I'll do to him.

552
00:28:19,360 --> 00:28:21,960
While I sit here polishing people's shoes,

553
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:23,620
my eyes are on his front door.

554
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:25,420
Don't judge me by my looks, Mr. Shamsali.

555
00:28:25,460 --> 00:28:27,280
Let the dust settle,

556
00:28:27,320 --> 00:28:29,180
I know how to pay him back.

557
00:28:29,220 --> 00:28:31,160
If I let him get away with it...

558
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:34,260
If I let him... But it's too soon. The time has to come.

559
00:28:34,300 --> 00:28:36,520
The time has to come.

560
00:28:37,269 --> 00:28:39,420
The time has to come.

561
00:28:39,460 --> 00:28:42,420
Houshang Khan, pay them no mind,

562
00:28:42,460 --> 00:28:44,420
because we have another mission.

563
00:28:44,460 --> 00:28:46,420
You do your own job.

564
00:28:46,460 --> 00:28:48,420
If we can't handle one Indian,

565
00:28:48,460 --> 00:28:50,420
we'll be left out in the cold.

566
00:28:50,460 --> 00:28:52,420
The other scoundrels will swallow us whole.

567
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:55,490
Yes, those other scoundrels.

568
00:28:55,850 --> 00:28:58,230
They're the ones who matter.

569
00:29:00,460 --> 00:29:02,460
Yes, they're the ones who matter.

570
00:29:07,550 --> 00:29:08,420
Saeid dear,

571
00:29:08,460 --> 00:29:10,420
tell Ghasem to bring a glass of sherbet

572
00:29:10,460 --> 00:29:12,460
for Houshang Khan.

573
00:29:13,220 --> 00:29:16,220
Dear Uncle, Mash Ghasem's in the cellar.

574
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:22,670
On your mother's life, you're not joking? Swear on my life!

575
00:29:23,300 --> 00:29:28,300
I swear on your life, we got shot in the Lorestan war.

576
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:31,610
We were in hospital six, seven months too.

577
00:29:31,940 --> 00:29:35,940
That's why our wife divorced us, see.

578
00:29:37,420 --> 00:29:38,980
You mean it's completely gone?

579
00:29:39,020 --> 00:29:40,980
As if it never was.

580
00:29:41,020 --> 00:29:42,980
Not even this much left.

581
00:29:43,020 --> 00:29:44,980
Nothing.

582
00:29:45,020 --> 00:29:49,020
The whole house has crumbled to its foundations.

583
00:29:50,030 --> 00:29:53,205
But, my boy, some medicine, a cure, something?

584
00:29:54,290 --> 00:30:00,020
What medicine? There has to be something left to cure, doesn't there?

585
00:30:01,570 --> 00:30:06,020
Oh, good Lord! Of all places, where did that shameless bullet have to hit?

586
00:30:07,830 --> 00:30:09,705
Curse this rotten luck!

587
00:30:11,930 --> 00:30:17,080
And to think of all the tales we told these Tehranis about Ghias Abadi manhood!

588
00:30:18,090 --> 00:30:20,240
Well, townsman, you stay here and have a pipe.

589
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:22,620
Drink your tea, we'll pop into the kitchen.

590
00:30:22,660 --> 00:30:24,780
Don't be shy, drink up, drink, drink.

591
00:30:24,820 --> 00:30:26,020
Enjoy, go on, drink.

592
00:30:26,060 --> 00:30:27,740
Yes, I'll drink.

593
00:30:37,020 --> 00:30:38,570
Mash Ghasem, so what happened?

594
00:30:38,620 --> 00:30:40,495
Moment, my boy.

595
00:30:43,020 --> 00:30:44,980
What happened, Ghasem? Did you talk to him?

596
00:30:45,020 --> 00:30:48,980
Yes, Sir, we talked a lot with our townsman about this and that.

597
00:30:49,020 --> 00:30:49,980
And?

598
00:30:50,020 --> 00:30:50,980
Why should I lie, Sir?

599
00:30:51,020 --> 00:30:54,780
The grave is this close! -Hurry up and tell us, come on!

600
00:30:54,830 --> 00:30:59,150
Truth is, we haven't dared tell our townsman about Lady Qamar's pregnancy yet.

601
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:03,810
He agreed right off, but the poor soul has a flaw.

602
00:31:03,860 --> 00:31:05,470
What flaw?

603
00:31:05,520 --> 00:31:07,150
Saving your presence.

604
00:31:07,200 --> 00:31:09,860
The whole house has crumbled to its foundations.

605
00:31:09,980 --> 00:31:10,790
Meaning what?

606
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:12,550
What's he getting at?

607
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:15,970
If I'm not mistaken, he's hit a San Francisco problem.

608
00:31:16,020 --> 00:31:18,890
Asdollah, will you talk rubbish to the grave?

609
00:31:18,940 --> 00:31:20,970
Moment, moment.

610
00:31:21,020 --> 00:31:24,360
Right now the wounded hero's closer to the grave than I am.

611
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:26,060
Cat and dog at it again!

612
00:31:26,100 --> 00:31:27,700
Let me hear what he's saying!

613
00:31:27,740 --> 00:31:29,640
Saving your presence, no offense,

614
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:31,400
seems he's not our townsman.

615
00:31:31,440 --> 00:31:32,880
Meaning what?

616
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,680
How is he not your townsman?

617
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:36,200
His name's Ghias Abadi,

618
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:38,060
but he's not from Ghias Abad of Qom.

619
00:31:38,100 --> 00:31:39,240
What are you saying?

620
00:31:39,280 --> 00:31:41,770
He got shot in the Lorestan war, in the...

621
00:31:41,820 --> 00:31:42,600
How to put it?

622
00:31:42,640 --> 00:31:45,040
What, are your townsmen bulletproof?

623
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:48,240
Don't Ghias Abadis get shot? Only we get shot?

624
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:52,180
You do, but not where this poor soul got hit.

625
00:31:52,220 --> 00:31:53,720
Where did he get hit?

626
00:31:53,760 --> 00:31:57,100
Well, well, in the guts and...

627
00:31:57,140 --> 00:32:01,860
Pardon my saying, in the guts... the poor soul has no guts at all.

628
00:32:01,900 --> 00:32:04,780
Mash Ghasem, how can a man have no guts?

629
00:32:04,820 --> 00:32:08,340
He doesn't! Didn't we say he's not our townsman?

630
00:32:08,380 --> 00:32:11,260
Then tell us what happened to his guts.

631
00:32:11,300 --> 00:32:16,300
Lady Aziz, you know Mash Ghasem's ways. The poor man's very shy.

632
00:32:17,300 --> 00:32:20,260
By guts he doesn't mean guts.

633
00:32:20,300 --> 00:32:22,500
Why don't you get what he means?

634
00:32:23,300 --> 00:32:25,260
Well, then what does he mean?

635
00:32:25,300 --> 00:32:31,260
Well, he means, he means that famous tower of San Francisco.

636
00:32:31,300 --> 00:32:33,260
The tower of San Francisco?

637
00:32:33,300 --> 00:32:35,260
Ugh, what a filthy mouth, Asdollah!

638
00:32:35,300 --> 00:32:39,260
No surprise. When a man has no shame, you can't expect better.

639
00:32:39,300 --> 00:32:41,300
Moment!

640
00:32:42,240 --> 00:32:47,150
You, the very monument to modesty, kindly tell us: that organ just mentioned,

641
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,260
what would you call it?

642
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:49,260
One doesn't name it.

643
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:53,260
Either you say its proper name, or you get it across by sign language.

644
00:32:53,300 --> 00:32:56,260
You can't very well call it a nose or an eye instead!

645
00:32:56,300 --> 00:32:57,260
What an ass you are!

646
00:32:57,300 --> 00:32:59,260
Come on, you ease off too.

647
00:32:59,300 --> 00:33:01,260
Whether he has one or not,

648
00:33:01,300 --> 00:33:04,260
what does that damned thing matter?

649
00:33:04,300 --> 00:33:07,700
Do you want them to grow old together?

650
00:33:07,740 --> 00:33:10,395
Oh! Shame on me! God forbid!

651
00:33:11,500 --> 00:33:15,100
The trouble is, this way you can't pin the baby on him.

652
00:33:15,140 --> 00:33:17,770
Why are you making such a production of it?

653
00:33:17,820 --> 00:33:20,420
Tell him it's only ten, fifteen days.

654
00:33:20,460 --> 00:33:22,660
After that he has to divorce her, mind.

655
00:33:22,700 --> 00:33:26,250
Make him see he gets some money, then he goes on his way.

656
00:33:26,300 --> 00:33:28,160
You act like the world owes you.

657
00:33:28,200 --> 00:33:31,340
People have their dignity. Have you looked at yourself?

658
00:33:31,380 --> 00:33:33,710
As if everyone's his father's servant.

659
00:33:35,880 --> 00:33:38,740
Mash Ghasem, you must tell him the truth straight out.

660
00:33:38,780 --> 00:33:41,960
Once the Aspiran knows we want to give him a wife,

661
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:45,340
he'll see for himself that guts are no issue at all.

662
00:33:45,380 --> 00:33:49,000
If there's no running to do, who cares if he's got legs or he's lame?

663
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:50,135
Yes.

664
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:52,920
Honestly, we're too embarrassed to tell him that.

665
00:33:52,960 --> 00:33:55,200
And you want us to break the news.

666
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:58,000
You don't know how touchy Ghias Abadis are about honor.

667
00:33:58,040 --> 00:33:59,660
We're afraid he'll raise hell.

668
00:33:59,700 --> 00:34:01,760
Ease him into it, Mash Ghasem.

669
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:05,400
Actually, better to spring it on him all at once.

670
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:08,260
Better if two people come with us to hold him down.

671
00:34:08,300 --> 00:34:10,695
Oh my! He might spill blood!

672
00:34:11,300 --> 00:34:13,435
I can't come,

673
00:34:14,060 --> 00:34:15,980
or else I'd go with you.

674
00:34:16,020 --> 00:34:16,820
Shall I?

675
00:34:16,860 --> 00:34:17,840
No, Madam.

676
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:21,660
We'd be ashamed to talk of such things in front of you.

677
00:34:21,700 --> 00:34:23,940
That leaves me and...

678
00:34:23,980 --> 00:34:25,080
you and...

679
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:25,820
Sir.

680
00:34:25,860 --> 00:34:28,600
Asdollah, a little shame wouldn't hurt.

681
00:34:30,500 --> 00:34:31,855
Mash Ghasem,

682
00:34:32,020 --> 00:34:33,460
come, you and I will go.

683
00:34:33,500 --> 00:34:35,880
No, Sir, you're not strong enough alone.

684
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:37,120
You, me and Saeid will go.

685
00:34:37,160 --> 00:34:38,800
Bless you, Asdollah.

686
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:42,260
For heaven's sake, don't tell him Qamar has money of her own!

687
00:34:42,300 --> 00:34:43,900
He'll get greedy.

688
00:34:43,940 --> 00:34:46,880
Don't worry, Lord Freeloader! Don't worry.

689
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:49,160
Qamar's late father's fortune is all yours.

690
00:34:49,200 --> 00:34:50,460
Sleep, hero.

691
00:34:50,500 --> 00:34:52,720
Sleep, you're in a bad way.

692
00:34:56,500 --> 00:34:57,820
Come on, Saeid, come.

693
00:34:57,860 --> 00:34:58,820
Where?

694
00:34:58,860 --> 00:35:02,295
You've heard everything and now you play dumb with us? Come on.

695
00:35:02,860 --> 00:35:05,820
Listen to me, you two, or there'll be bloodshed.

696
00:35:05,860 --> 00:35:09,820
When we cough, you'll know we're about to tell him the main thing.

697
00:35:09,860 --> 00:35:10,820
Hold his shoulders.

698
00:35:10,860 --> 00:35:13,450
Hold on till we've told him all, or we'll have to run.

699
00:35:13,500 --> 00:35:14,820
But he's not even strong.

700
00:35:14,860 --> 00:35:18,820
You're a kid, my boy. Spilling blood isn't about size.

701
00:35:18,860 --> 00:35:20,820
He's a Ghias Abadi. We had a townsman...

702
00:35:20,860 --> 00:35:23,580
Well, tell us the rest later. Let's go.

703
00:35:30,860 --> 00:35:31,820
Excuse me, Sir.

704
00:35:31,860 --> 00:35:32,980
Hello, dear.

705
00:35:33,020 --> 00:35:33,820
Humble spread.

706
00:35:33,860 --> 00:35:35,820
Please, Mr. Aspiran.

707
00:35:35,860 --> 00:35:38,820
Why stand on ceremony? There's none of that between us.

708
00:35:38,860 --> 00:35:40,280
Please.

709
00:35:42,860 --> 00:35:45,820
So, Mr. Aspiran, you're well, God willing?

710
00:35:45,860 --> 00:35:47,820
Oh, thanks to you, not bad.

711
00:35:47,860 --> 00:35:48,820
How's your mother?

712
00:35:48,860 --> 00:35:49,820
She prays for you, sir.

713
00:35:49,860 --> 00:35:51,980
So, what's new at the office?

714
00:35:52,020 --> 00:35:53,420
Seems you're very busy.

715
00:35:53,460 --> 00:35:58,720
Yes, sir, that's right. They send me on one mission after another.

716
00:35:58,760 --> 00:36:01,460
Yes, and such difficult missions!

717
00:36:01,500 --> 00:36:03,260
Pardon me, sir.

718
00:36:03,300 --> 00:36:05,750
Carry on, Mr. Aspiran.

719
00:36:05,800 --> 00:36:07,440
Mmm! What a smell!

720
00:36:07,480 --> 00:36:09,740
Yesh, it'sh top-grade shtuff.

721
00:36:09,780 --> 00:36:11,300
Shall I offer you some?

722
00:36:11,340 --> 00:36:12,565
Thanks.

723
00:36:12,860 --> 00:36:14,960
You don't partake?

724
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:16,660
Now and then, for fun.

725
00:36:16,700 --> 00:36:18,240
Thanks, you go ahead.

726
00:36:18,280 --> 00:36:23,620
I'm delighted to be with one of the police's finesht officers.

727
00:36:23,660 --> 00:36:25,520
Congratulations, Mr. Aspiran.

728
00:36:25,560 --> 00:36:29,200
Our Lady Qamar has seen you and taken a liking to you.

729
00:36:30,060 --> 00:36:31,840
Her parents agree too.

730
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:35,020
Bless you, you're still young. You shouldn't stay single.

731
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:37,780
I'm your humble servant.

732
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:41,020
But there was something we told Mash Ghasem.

733
00:36:41,060 --> 00:36:44,360
I mean, a secret we told Mash Ghasem.

734
00:36:44,400 --> 00:36:46,380
Moment, Mr. Aspiran.

735
00:36:46,420 --> 00:36:48,080
That's nothing important.

736
00:36:48,120 --> 00:36:50,360
A thousand things happen to a man in war.

737
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:53,880
Plenty of people had such trouble and got cured,

738
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,860
with today's equipment,

739
00:36:55,900 --> 00:36:57,920
with all the progress medicine has made.

740
00:36:57,960 --> 00:37:00,000
But, sir, ours can't be cured.

741
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:01,135
Yes.

742
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:04,060
Seems nothing's left of them.

743
00:37:07,360 --> 00:37:09,380
Just bad luck, that's all.

744
00:37:09,420 --> 00:37:12,550
If you'll take it like this, we've no objection.

745
00:37:12,600 --> 00:37:15,520
But tomorrow her mother, the relatives,

746
00:37:15,560 --> 00:37:18,605
the lady herself mustn't say, "You never told us."

747
00:37:19,560 --> 00:37:21,520
Her parents must accept it.

748
00:37:21,560 --> 00:37:24,800
They've no choice. Qamar wants you.

749
00:37:25,560 --> 00:37:29,520
The girl agrees, the parents agree, and now you play hard to get?

750
00:37:29,560 --> 00:37:32,520
But I want to shush something out.

751
00:37:32,560 --> 00:37:33,520
Lord have mercy!

752
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:36,520
What's that, townsman? You want us to shush?

753
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:37,850
About what?

754
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:42,479
We want to know why they want to give a girl to us.

755
00:37:42,600 --> 00:37:47,540
In all of Tehran, there'sh nobody more eligible than us?

756
00:37:49,820 --> 00:37:51,175
Mash Ghasem!

757
00:37:54,160 --> 00:37:56,160
Mash Ghasem!

758
00:38:16,360 --> 00:38:17,520
What?

759
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:23,040
The bride's pregnant.

760
00:38:32,100 --> 00:38:37,000
Ah... so the apple's rotten, or it'd never have fallen in our lap.

761
00:38:38,280 --> 00:38:41,100
Well, well, bravo! You've got it.

762
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:43,520
We'd caught on from the start.

763
00:38:43,560 --> 00:38:45,520
Spineless slob!

764
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:47,520
Bravo, Mr. Aspiran!

765
00:38:47,560 --> 00:38:50,470
What brains, what wit!

766
00:38:50,520 --> 00:38:52,135
You've got it.

767
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:53,520
This poor girl

768
00:38:53,560 --> 00:38:56,150
apparently went to the men's bathhouse once,

769
00:38:56,200 --> 00:38:57,520
and by bad luck, in there,

770
00:38:57,560 --> 00:38:59,520
she got pregnant.

771
00:38:59,560 --> 00:39:01,520
The men's bathhouse

772
00:39:01,560 --> 00:39:02,610
is a very bad thing.

773
00:39:02,650 --> 00:39:04,120
You know all about it.

774
00:39:04,160 --> 00:39:07,560
Shame on a spineless man, townsman!

775
00:39:07,740 --> 00:39:08,965
Nothing.

776
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:11,520
Seems that's how it happened.

777
00:39:11,560 --> 00:39:12,520
Spineless!

778
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:14,520
What did you say, townsman?

779
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:16,520
We mean, that's how she got pregnant.

780
00:39:16,560 --> 00:39:17,520
Yes, it doesn't matter.

781
00:39:17,560 --> 00:39:20,290
So we're to marry this lady

782
00:39:20,340 --> 00:39:22,735
and divorce her after a while?

783
00:39:22,880 --> 00:39:25,510
Yes, maybe ten or fifteen days later.

784
00:39:25,560 --> 00:39:28,290
Ten or fifteen days won't do.

785
00:39:29,300 --> 00:39:31,490
Everyone will find out.

786
00:39:31,540 --> 00:39:33,600
We have our reputation.

787
00:39:33,820 --> 00:39:35,520
At least three months,

788
00:39:35,560 --> 00:39:38,560
then we'll cook up some excuse.

789
00:39:39,540 --> 00:39:41,460
Fine, what's the difference?

790
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:44,600
The point is for this match to go ahead with every blessing.

791
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:46,320
Mr. Aspiran has said yes,

792
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:48,660
and Lady Qamar is madly in love with him.

793
00:39:48,700 --> 00:39:49,520
So, fine for now.

794
00:39:49,560 --> 00:39:50,930
Three months later, divorce.

795
00:39:50,980 --> 00:39:51,650
Well, yes.

796
00:39:51,700 --> 00:39:54,940
But, sir, I must tell you that...

797
00:39:54,980 --> 00:39:56,540
How shall I put it, honestly...

798
00:39:56,580 --> 00:39:57,560
No, go on, go on.

799
00:39:57,600 --> 00:39:59,085
It's wartime, after all.

800
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:01,695
Our wages are two months behind.

801
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:04,060
Until when? God knows.

802
00:40:04,100 --> 00:40:07,160
If I had shome cash in hand,

803
00:40:07,780 --> 00:40:08,860
I wouldn't mention it.

804
00:40:08,900 --> 00:40:12,240
Yes, prices are high. It'll cost two thousand tomans,

805
00:40:12,280 --> 00:40:14,000
with all the comings and goings.

806
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:16,420
Exshpenses are no joke.

807
00:40:18,340 --> 00:40:19,360
Well, yes, you...

808
00:40:19,400 --> 00:40:21,020
you're quite right, you are.

809
00:40:21,060 --> 00:40:22,540
You're doing a good deed.

810
00:40:22,580 --> 00:40:25,170
You shouldn't have to pay the expenses as well.

811
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:27,605
All the expenses are on

812
00:40:27,780 --> 00:40:29,040
the girl's mother.

813
00:40:29,080 --> 00:40:31,400
Because if there's any flaw here,

814
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:33,680
it's on Qamar's side.

815
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:38,480
When you're done, come upstairs with Mash Ghasem.

816
00:40:38,520 --> 00:40:39,840
I'll cover the expenses, OK?

817
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:41,100
I'm your humble servant.

818
00:40:41,140 --> 00:40:42,420
Good man, Aspiran!

819
00:40:42,460 --> 00:40:43,700
Up, let's go. Saeid, let's go.

820
00:40:43,740 --> 00:40:44,980
Goodbye.

821
00:40:45,020 --> 00:40:45,820
Congrats!

822
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:47,735
We're coming, Sir.

823
00:40:48,620 --> 00:40:52,260
What a greedy so-and-so! The shameless man wants two thousand tomans!

824
00:40:52,300 --> 00:40:54,140
Honestly, he's worth it, Lady Aziz.

825
00:40:54,180 --> 00:40:56,340
You'll never find one cheaper.

826
00:40:56,380 --> 00:40:59,000
It's wartime, there may be a famine.

827
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:02,810
You could at least have haggled.

828
00:41:02,860 --> 00:41:04,030
Haggle over what?

829
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:04,870
The price is fair.

830
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:06,890
Oh, stop clowning around.

831
00:41:06,940 --> 00:41:11,180
Well, townsman, if your craving's eased, come, let's go upstairs.

832
00:41:16,180 --> 00:41:16,910
After you, then.

833
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:17,870
No, after you.

834
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:19,030
Lead the way, please.

835
00:41:19,080 --> 00:41:21,250
Don't stand on ceremony. Please.

836
00:41:31,080 --> 00:41:32,980
Damn him, he's setting terms too?

837
00:41:33,020 --> 00:41:36,200
Once this girl's business is done, I'll show him who's boss.

838
00:41:36,240 --> 00:41:38,540
To hell with that bald head of his!

839
00:41:38,580 --> 00:41:40,560
All right, enough.

840
00:41:40,600 --> 00:41:42,360
Heavens, Lady Aziz is coming.

841
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:43,400
After you.

842
00:41:43,440 --> 00:41:44,750
Not at all, after you.

843
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:45,470
Mr. Aspiran.

844
00:41:45,520 --> 00:41:46,440
Hello, Mr. Aspiran.

845
00:41:46,480 --> 00:41:47,580
Peace be upon you.

846
00:41:47,620 --> 00:41:49,100
Welcome.

847
00:41:49,140 --> 00:41:50,800
This is Qamar's father.

848
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:52,420
He's had a little accident.

849
00:41:52,460 --> 00:41:53,700
Come in, come in.

850
00:41:53,740 --> 00:41:55,460
Please sit down, please, I beg you.

851
00:41:55,500 --> 00:41:58,545
Sir, God forbid, did you fall off the roof?

852
00:41:59,140 --> 00:42:00,960
No, it's... strategic.

853
00:42:02,380 --> 00:42:03,000
Mr. Aspiran,

854
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:05,120
I hope you realize

855
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:06,520
that it's a respectable,

856
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:08,700
aristocratic family

857
00:42:08,740 --> 00:42:10,110
you're marrying into.

858
00:42:10,160 --> 00:42:11,320
Yes.

859
00:42:11,540 --> 00:42:13,140
Your appearance

860
00:42:13,180 --> 00:42:14,980
and behavior mustn't be

861
00:42:15,020 --> 00:42:16,780
such that, God forbid,

862
00:42:16,820 --> 00:42:18,240
they damage their reputation.

863
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:19,960
I'm your humble servant.

864
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:22,680
I'll behave however you say.

865
00:42:22,720 --> 00:42:24,010
Thank you.

866
00:42:24,580 --> 00:42:26,910
Lady Aziz, about the house,

867
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:28,600
given it any thought?

868
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:31,440
Goodness, how could I part with my child?

869
00:42:31,480 --> 00:42:33,840
Mr. Ghias Abadi must come live at our house.

870
00:42:33,880 --> 00:42:36,620
The upstairs room is empty, I'll get it ready for him.

871
00:42:36,660 --> 00:42:39,200
Well, Madam, we have an old mother

872
00:42:39,240 --> 00:42:40,680
we can't leave alone.

873
00:42:40,720 --> 00:42:42,778
Well, bring your mother along too.

874
00:42:42,828 --> 00:42:44,180
Asdollah, what rubbish!

875
00:42:44,220 --> 00:42:45,520
In our house? How?

876
00:42:45,560 --> 00:42:48,480
Moment! There's no other way, dear Dustali.

877
00:42:48,520 --> 00:42:52,000
Mr. Ghias Abadi can't leave his old, ailing mother alone.

878
00:42:52,040 --> 00:42:53,380
Can you, Mr. Ghias Abadi?

879
00:42:53,420 --> 00:42:54,220
No, sir.

880
00:42:54,260 --> 00:42:55,240
He can't.

881
00:42:55,280 --> 00:42:59,040
All we have in this world is an old, frail mother

882
00:42:59,080 --> 00:43:00,900
and a widowed shishter.

883
00:43:00,940 --> 00:43:01,980
Really?

884
00:43:02,020 --> 00:43:03,115
Yes.

885
00:43:04,448 --> 00:43:05,920
You have a sister too?

886
00:43:05,960 --> 00:43:06,978
Yes.

887
00:43:07,028 --> 00:43:08,940
What does she do? How old is she?

888
00:43:08,980 --> 00:43:11,520
Well, sir, we married her off two years ago.

889
00:43:11,560 --> 00:43:14,150
Last year her husband got run over by a car.

890
00:43:14,848 --> 00:43:17,373
Now she shings in a café.

891
00:43:17,988 --> 00:43:19,560
In a café? Ooh!

892
00:43:19,600 --> 00:43:21,020
Yes, Madam.

893
00:43:21,328 --> 00:43:23,600
How can I stop people talking?

894
00:43:23,640 --> 00:43:25,820
Well, Mr. Aspiran can leave his sister behind.

895
00:43:25,860 --> 00:43:27,400
Well, well!

896
00:43:27,440 --> 00:43:28,280
Bravo!

897
00:43:28,320 --> 00:43:30,080
Splendid!

898
00:43:30,120 --> 00:43:31,300
Lady Aziz,

899
00:43:31,340 --> 00:43:33,420
Mr. Ghias Abadi won't hear of it.

900
00:43:33,460 --> 00:43:35,540
A young widow

901
00:43:35,580 --> 00:43:37,688
can't be left on her own in Tehran.

902
00:43:37,728 --> 00:43:38,528
Yes.

903
00:43:38,568 --> 00:43:39,798
There he goes again.

904
00:43:39,848 --> 00:43:41,540
God curse you, Dustali!

905
00:43:41,580 --> 00:43:44,838
Who'll be able to look the relatives in the eye now?

906
00:43:44,888 --> 00:43:47,620
Asdollah, will you shut that wretched mouth?

907
00:43:47,660 --> 00:43:49,800
Moment, moment.

908
00:43:49,840 --> 00:43:54,460
You mean Mr. Aspiran should abandon his mother and sister in this huge city

909
00:43:54,500 --> 00:43:56,300
and live with you like a kept son-in-law?

910
00:43:56,340 --> 00:44:00,260
Would Mr. Aspiran's pride allow it? Is it a joke? He can't. Never.

911
00:44:00,300 --> 00:44:02,500
Can you, Mr. Aspiran? So much the better.

912
00:44:02,540 --> 00:44:04,935
What's it to me, anyway?

913
00:44:05,228 --> 00:44:07,280
No, sir, seems the gentleman doesn't like us.

914
00:44:07,320 --> 00:44:09,700
We can't do as the gentleman says

915
00:44:09,740 --> 00:44:12,180
and abandon our sister and mother to fate.

916
00:44:12,220 --> 00:44:14,030
We'll take our leave.

917
00:44:14,588 --> 00:44:16,980
Hey, where are you going, townsman? Sit down.

918
00:44:17,020 --> 00:44:20,100
The gentleman's words don't count. You talk to the lady.

919
00:44:20,140 --> 00:44:22,700
Well, what choice is there? I have to accept.

920
00:44:22,740 --> 00:44:26,440
For this poor child of mine, I'll do anything.

921
00:44:26,480 --> 00:44:28,440
What a circus!

922
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:30,440
Aziz, do you know what you're saying?

923
00:44:30,480 --> 00:44:34,440
The Aspiran, his old mother and his singer sister in our house?

924
00:44:34,480 --> 00:44:37,440
No, sir, with your permission, I'll take my leave.

925
00:44:37,480 --> 00:44:38,440
Oh, Mash Ghasem!

926
00:44:38,480 --> 00:44:40,440
Townsman, for heaven's sake!

927
00:44:40,480 --> 00:44:43,440
He won't turn you down, Mash Ghasem.

928
00:44:43,480 --> 00:44:46,440
Sit, dear, sit down, Mr. Ghias Abadi.

929
00:44:46,480 --> 00:44:49,440
Sir, I won't hear my mother and sister insulted.

930
00:44:49,480 --> 00:44:52,900
Dustali, if you don't shut up, we'll have to investigate again

931
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:54,580
to find the baby's real father.

932
00:44:54,620 --> 00:44:55,900
What's it to me, anyway?

933
00:44:55,940 --> 00:44:59,940
She's the mother. Do whatever you see fit, what's it to me?

934
00:45:00,508 --> 00:45:02,958
Do whatever damn thing you like.

935
00:45:03,008 --> 00:45:05,200
Honestly, I don't know what to do with myself.

936
00:45:05,240 --> 00:45:07,480
Whatever you say, Asdollah.

937
00:45:09,440 --> 00:45:11,830
They say let's set the wedding for Thursday night.

938
00:45:11,870 --> 00:45:13,200
All right, Mr. Aspiran?

939
00:45:13,240 --> 00:45:18,980
Well, for us Ghias Abadis, respecting your mother comes before your daily bread.

940
00:45:19,020 --> 00:45:23,460
First we must tell our mother we've found a girl we like,

941
00:45:23,500 --> 00:45:24,960
sho she can ashk for her hand.

942
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:28,140
Yes, yes, good, absolutely necessary.

943
00:45:28,180 --> 00:45:29,720
Couldn't she come tonight?

944
00:45:29,760 --> 00:45:31,460
Bring your sister along too, mind.

945
00:45:31,500 --> 00:45:33,380
We're family now, after all.

946
00:45:33,420 --> 00:45:36,560
Yes, sir. Then we'd better go before it gets late.

947
00:45:36,600 --> 00:45:37,400
Yes, yes.

948
00:45:37,440 --> 00:45:40,960
As it happens, my sister has no show at the café tonight.

949
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:42,960
Well, well! How wonderful!

950
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:43,960
How wonderful.

951
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:46,460
Seems it's all coming together, oh my!

952
00:45:46,648 --> 00:45:50,960
But, sir, that matter I mentioned about the Lorestan war

953
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:52,960
must stay between us, sir.

954
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:53,960
Of course, of course.

955
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:57,305
Nobody in the world knows about this business of ours.

956
00:45:57,808 --> 00:46:01,960
If one day, someday, it ever comes out somewhere,

957
00:46:02,000 --> 00:46:05,960
both your daughter's reputation and ours will be ruined.

958
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:07,960
Bless you, you're very kind.

959
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:08,960
Goodbye.

960
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:09,960
Goodbye.

961
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:12,000
After you, after you.

962
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:15,950
Mr. Aspiran, have your mother come this afternoon,

963
00:46:16,000 --> 00:46:17,960
together with your sister.

964
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:19,960
Yes, sir, certainly.

965
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:21,960
I have a word for you, sir.

966
00:46:22,000 --> 00:46:23,960
For me? Go on, dear.

967
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:26,998
Don't mention Lady Qamar's pregnancy in front of my mother.

968
00:46:27,048 --> 00:46:28,918
If she finds out, she'll never agree.

969
00:46:28,968 --> 00:46:29,960
No, I won't say that.

970
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:31,960
I'll talk to her in such a way

971
00:46:32,000 --> 00:46:33,950
that she'll agree at once. Leave it to me.

972
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:36,500
Thank you very much.

973
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:19,800
Long live Mr. Ghias Abadi! Bless you!

974
00:47:19,850 --> 00:47:21,088
Long live the Aspiran!

975
00:47:21,128 --> 00:47:21,958
Bless you.

976
00:47:22,008 --> 00:47:24,740
At your service, at your service.

977
00:47:25,048 --> 00:47:26,598
Your humble servant.

978
00:47:37,008 --> 00:47:39,078
The wig problem's solved too.

979
00:47:39,128 --> 00:47:43,878
We'll go to Lalehzar Street and buy him a nice wig, so Qamar won't be put off.

980
00:47:43,928 --> 00:47:45,198
Well, let's go.

981
00:47:45,248 --> 00:47:48,163
And you go see about Qamar's dress.

982
00:47:49,808 --> 00:47:53,070
Oh no, my head!

983
00:47:56,008 --> 00:47:57,363
Ow, my head!

984
00:48:00,568 --> 00:48:01,923
What's wrong with him?

985
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:04,960
For now, Dustali, hand over the money for the wig.

986
00:48:05,000 --> 00:48:06,960
I'm to pay for the wig?

987
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:07,960
Don't, if you'd rather not.

988
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:09,960
Then Qamar won't marry this bald fellow,

989
00:48:10,000 --> 00:48:13,960
and we'll have to set out again and hunt for the baby's real father,

990
00:48:14,000 --> 00:48:15,960
so he can come and marry the baby's mother.

991
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:19,960
Asdollah, on my father's soul, say that again and I'll skin you alive!

992
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:20,960
Moment!

993
00:48:21,000 --> 00:48:21,960
Moment!

994
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:23,960
I don't get it.

995
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:25,960
Why did you take offense?

996
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:30,160
I said we'd have to set out and find that disgraceful, unconscionable,

997
00:48:30,260 --> 00:48:32,090
good-for-nothing father of the baby.

998
00:48:32,140 --> 00:48:33,910
Why did your face go all red like that?

999
00:48:33,960 --> 00:48:37,090
Don't tell me, you sly dog, you went to San Francisco with her yourself!

1000
00:48:37,140 --> 00:48:39,540
Stop, you son of a dog!

1001
00:48:39,840 --> 00:48:42,625
Stop, will you, you shameless lowlife!

1002
00:48:42,840 --> 00:48:44,510
Lying bastard!

1003
00:48:44,560 --> 00:48:46,190
Trying to trick me?

1004
00:48:46,240 --> 00:48:50,240
You strapped this rag on your head to swindle me?

1005
00:48:51,960 --> 00:48:53,705
Dishonorable scum!

1006
00:49:33,880 --> 00:49:35,910
Saeid. Saeid.

1007
00:49:35,960 --> 00:49:37,575
Yes, Agha Jan.

1008
00:49:39,560 --> 00:49:42,210
What's all this coming and going today?

1009
00:49:42,260 --> 00:49:44,810
They brought a carriage to meet Pouri at the station, who-

1010
00:49:44,860 --> 00:49:46,050
I know all that.

1011
00:49:46,100 --> 00:49:49,810
Over there, at that Dear Uncle Napoleon of yours.

1012
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:50,960
Nothing, Agha Jan.

1013
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:54,960
What do you mean, nothing? I heard Nayeb Teymoor-Khan was here today.

1014
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:57,000
What's going on?

1015
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:01,960
They're all caught up in Qamar's pregnancy.

1016
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:03,960
What was that fellow doing here?

1017
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:07,305
He's the Nayeb's deputy. He just went out with Mash Ghasem.

1018
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:10,960
Actually, they want to marry Qamar off.

1019
00:50:11,000 --> 00:50:13,960
Marry her off? To whom?

1020
00:50:14,000 --> 00:50:14,960
To the Aspiran.

1021
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:16,960
Who?

1022
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:18,960
Aspiran Ghias Abadi.

1023
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:20,225
Lovely.

1024
00:50:20,280 --> 00:50:25,000
The cream of the nation's aristocracy in the arms of Aspiran Ghias Abadi!

1025
00:50:27,200 --> 00:50:29,020
Congratulations to them!

1026
00:50:43,180 --> 00:50:44,600
Goodbye.

